WEBVTT

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:09.978
<v><b>Speaker:</b></v> We all know that too much sugar and salt isn't good for us.

00:00:10.858 --> 00:00:15.128
But do we really know how much sugar and salt are in

00:00:15.129 --> 00:00:18.341
some of the things we eat and drink every day?

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:21.670
Let’s start with sugar.

00:00:23.194 --> 00:00:28.166
According to the American Heart Association, the maximum healthy limit

00:00:28.190 --> 00:00:35.540
for a woman is 24 grams of sugar a day. That’s just 6 teaspoons.

00:00:37.061 --> 00:00:43.399
For a man, it is no more than 36 grams, which is 9 teaspoons.

00:00:46.407 --> 00:00:54.924
Here we have an egg, a can of soda, a small bar of dark chocolate, and an apple.

00:00:56.398 --> 00:00:58.986
How much sugar do you think they contain?

00:01:01.914 --> 00:01:05.200
One of them has 35 grams of sugar.

00:01:06.143 --> 00:01:10.835
That’s 11 grams more than the healthy limit for a woman in a day.

00:01:13.317 --> 00:01:14.917
Which one do you think it is?

00:01:17.091 --> 00:01:19.584
Yes, it’s the can of soda.

00:01:20.939 --> 00:01:27.801
A can of soda has approximately 35 grams of sugar. That’s a lot.

00:01:30.454 --> 00:01:32.029
And which has no sugar?

00:01:35.368 --> 00:01:37.116
Of course, it’s the egg.

00:01:38.712 --> 00:01:40.727
So what about the other two?

00:01:42.088 --> 00:01:48.142
Which do you think has more sugar, the chocolate or the apple?

00:01:49.822 --> 00:01:52.324
Surprisingly, it’s the apple.

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:59.817
The apple has approximately 23 grams of sugar. That’s a lot.

00:02:01.263 --> 00:02:04.378
But it's fructose, a natural sugar.

00:02:06.113 --> 00:02:12.241
And remember that fruit is also good for you, because it contains vitamin C.

00:02:14.298 --> 00:02:19.483
The chocolate bar only has a little sugar, just 10 grams.

00:02:20.842 --> 00:02:25.480
But remember: it’s dark chocolate, and it’s only a small bar.

00:02:29.662 --> 00:02:33.572
What about salt? How much salt can we eat a day?

00:02:37.024 --> 00:02:39.972
This time it's the same for men and women.

00:02:41.334 --> 00:02:44.456
The answer is no more than 6 grams.

00:02:47.188 --> 00:02:52.620
Here we have a small bag of chips, a bottle of olive oil,

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:57.996
a bottle of water, and a piece of bread.

00:03:00.004 --> 00:03:02.514
So how much salt do they contain?

00:03:04.156 --> 00:03:08.674
Which one has a lot of salt, and which one has none?

00:03:10.495 --> 00:03:15.167
You may be surprised to hear that the one with a lot of salt is

00:03:16.332 --> 00:03:18.112
the piece of white bread.

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:23.004
It has approximately 0.5 grams.

00:03:24.846 --> 00:03:26.801
And which one has no salt?

00:03:28.662 --> 00:03:32.816
No, it’s not the water, it’s

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:34.950
the olive oil.

00:03:35.856 --> 00:03:43.602
It contains no salt, and as part of a Mediterranean diet, it’s very healthy.

00:03:44.982 --> 00:03:46.915
So what about the other two?

00:03:48.096 --> 00:03:54.494
Well, a small bag of chips has approximately 0.34 grams of salt.

00:03:56.571 --> 00:04:00.026
And lastly, there is a little in the water.

00:04:01.266 --> 00:04:05.199
Just 0.0023 grams.

00:04:07.746 --> 00:04:11.320
So when you’re shopping, how do you know what to buy

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:14.746
to make sure it doesn’t have too much sugar or salt?

00:04:16.475 --> 00:04:23.333
The answer is, always check the list of ingredients, and remember what your daily limit is.